@nsobid-F19B2E01E1794F933A9720C1404BB6F6

# Bayonetta 2 1.2 - 2048x2048 shadow resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Sharpens the sun shadow. The engine renders two 1024x1024 cascades into one
// 1024x2048 depth atlas, stacked vertically; it becomes a 2048x4096 atlas of two
// 2048x2048 cascades. The colour target bound with the atlas during the caster
// pass is resized to match.
//
// The caster pass places each cascade with an explicit viewport, cascade 0 at
// y = 0 and cascade 1 at y = one cascade height. Those viewports scale with the
// atlas, so each cascade stays the same fraction of it, which is what the
// receiver shaders sample by. Nothing else hardcodes the size: the sampling
// view is created from the same constants patched here.
//
// REQUIRES one of the [WxH] resolution mods. The shadow textures live in the
// same fixed render-target pool as the G-buffers and grow it by about 48 MB,
// which the stock 128 MB pool cannot absorb. The resolution mods own that pool
// and already size it for this mod; do NOT copy their offsets here.

@enabled
// Cascade atlas depth texture and its sampling view, 1024x2048 -> 2048x4096.
0097D0AC 01008152   // MOVZ W1,#2048 (was 1024)
0097D0B0 02008252   // MOVZ W2,#4096 (was 2048)
0097D0D4 02008152   // MOVZ W2,#2048 (was 1024)
0097D0E0 03008252   // MOVZ W3,#4096 (was 2048)
// Colour target bound alongside the atlas in the caster pass.
0097DFE4 01008152   // MOVZ W1,#2048 (was 1024)
0097DFE8 02008252   // MOVZ W2,#4096 (was 2048)
// Per-cascade viewport in the caster pass.
0097814C 01008152   // cascade 1 y offset (was 1024)
00978154 02008152   // cascade 1 width  (was 1024)
00978158 03008152   // cascade 1 height (was 1024)
00978168 02008152   // cascade 0 width  (was 1024)
00978170 03008152   // cascade 0 height (was 1024)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Bayonetta 2 1.2 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_010, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
